W44-AUDIT-8 Phase 7 e9 env-disable bisect

Run timestamp: 2026-05-24
Encoder commit: 8110e04f (Phase 5b shipped — extra_dc_precision=1 at e≤7;
                            Phase 6 QuantizeWP opt-in)
Reference: cjxl 0.12.0 (libjxl main build)

Worst e9 SSIM2-deficit cell: clic_22ea12 e9 d=4 (-3.54 SSIM2 vs cjxl).
Phase 5 fix is gated at effort ≤ 7 (libjxl `nl_dc = speed_tier < kFalcon`
parity), so the e9 cluster is structurally untouched by Phase 5.

Variants tested (20 = 1 baseline + 19 env hooks toggled OFF / forced):

  - BASELINE (no env)
  - JXL_W44_117_DISABLE=1                       (EPF seed in buttloop)
  - JXL_W44_120_EPF_SEED_MIN_DISTANCE=99        (W44-120 distance gate)
  - JXL_W44_AUDIT_5_P3_DISABLE=1                (AUDIT-5 Mode D opt-in)
  - JXL_W44_AUDIT_6_DISABLE=1                   (AUDIT-6 M3 gate)
  - JXL_W44_156_DISABLE=1                       (variant Z distance-aware)
  - JXL_W44_AUDIT_8_P6_FORCE_QUANTIZE_WP=1      (Phase 6 QuantizeWP shape)
  - JXL_W44_176_DISABLE=1                       (buttloop iter-count tuning)
  - JXL_W44_142_SUPPRESS_DISABLE=1              (W44-142 photo-suppress)
  - JXL_W44_152_DISABLE=1                       (W44-152 narrow-band lift)
  - JXL_W44_151_DISABLE=1                       (W44-151 high-mask gate)
  - JXL_W44_166_VARIANT_Z_ADMIT_MODE=off        (W44-166 variant Z admit)
  - JXL_W44_167_MODE=off                        (W44-167 per-m3 split)
  - JXL_W44_168_MODE=off                        (W44-168 Mode D LC)
  - JXL_W44_171_FORCE_TRIAL_ALL_EFFORTS=1       (DC tree trial all efforts)
  - JXL_W44_172_FORCE_VARIABLE_AT_E8=1          (DC tree Variable at e8)
  - __JXL_W44_57_FORCE_VARIABLE=1               (DC tree Variable forced)
  - __JXL_W44_57_FORCE_FIXED=1                  (DC tree kWPFixedDC forced)
  - JXL_W44_201_FORCE_LEGACY_LARGE_BUCKETS=1    (coeff-order legacy large)
  - JXL_W44_205_FORCE_LEGACY_MEDIUM_BUCKETS=1   (coeff-order legacy medium)

VERDICT (all 20 variants): SSIM2 is BYTE-IDENTICAL across every variant
(ours_ssim2 = 66.5687 on every row). ours_bfly = 3.8689 on every row.
ours_bytes differs on 3 hooks (W44_57_FORCE_FIXED: 33504, W44_201: 32941,
W44_205: 32689 — all entropy-coding tweaks that don't change decoded pixels).

CONCLUSION: NONE of the recent W44-* discriminator hooks are responsible
for the e9 SSIM2 deficit cluster. The deficit must originate in pipeline
machinery that fires uniformly across all our paths (and Phase 5's
extra_dc_precision=1 lift is OFF at e≥8).

Follow-on: the buttloop-isolation bench (sibling file
`w44_audit_8_phase7_e9_buttloop_isolate_2026-05-24.tsv`) tests
`with_butteraugli_iters(0)` at e9 to determine whether the buttloop
itself is the cliff source.

Reproducer:
  cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release \
    --features "parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop __expert" \
    --example w44_audit_8_phase7_e9_env_bisect

Files:
  jxl-encoder/examples/w44_audit_8_phase7_e9_env_bisect.rs
  benchmarks/w44_audit_8_phase7_e9_env_bisect_2026-05-24.tsv (this dataset)
